From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] winex11: don't flush the display for each memory DC's GC

Purpose: paint the XP shell's themed parts with fewer trips to the X
server, so that windows resize smoothly, notably in virtual machines.
Wine before: create_x11_physdev, which every CreateCompatibleDC calls,
created an X GC and flushed gdi_display. TransparentBlt creates two memory
DCs each time and uxtheme one for each theme part it draws, so each step of
a Luna window's resize flushed dozens of times and woke the X server each
time: a fifth of the time of the proxy, which paints the bridge's frames,
while resizing one.
Change: leave the GC's creation in the request buffer. Every request that
uses the GC goes out later on the same connection, after it.
Evidence: a profile of the proxy while Mousepad's frame is resized on Xvfb:
CreateCompatibleDC went from 22% of its time to 2.5% (XFlush from it from
19% to none); of 100 steps of the drag, 46-64 sizes were taken (38-51
before).
Scope: only with WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL.
---
 dlls/winex11.drv/init.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/init.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/init.c
index 09ef2bf..8263038 100644
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/init.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/init.c
@@ -33,6 +33,7 @@
 #include "x11drv.h"
 #include "xcomposite.h"
 #include "wine/debug.h"
+#include "wine/win4wine.h"
 
 WINE_DEFAULT_DEBUG_CHANNEL(x11drv);
 
@@ -90,7 +91,10 @@ static X11DRV_PDEVICE *create_x11_physdev( Drawable drawable )
     physDev->gc = XCreateGC( gdi_display, drawable, 0, NULL );
     XSetGraphicsExposures( gdi_display, physDev->gc, False );
     XSetSubwindowMode( gdi_display, physDev->gc, IncludeInferiors );
-    XFlush( gdi_display );
+    /* Every request using the GC goes out on gdi_display after these ones.
+     * Themed painting creates memory DCs by the dozen (TransparentBlt makes
+     * two each time), and each flush here woke the X server for nothing. */
+    if (!win4wine_external_shell()) XFlush( gdi_display );
     return physDev;
 }
 
